sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch12-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The form of a single-chambered foraminiferal shell is explained by the laws of surface tension: the protoplasm behaves as a fluid drop whose equilibrium shape is fixed when it acquires its solid covering.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Single-chambered foraminiferal shells take the form of fluid drops under surface tension";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XII, “The Spiral Shells of the Foraminifera”; topic “Foraminiferal shells as fluid drops”. Scope: unilocular Foraminifera (e.g. Orbulina, Lagena)"
}
